WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:01.200
- I heard this crazy story.

00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:03.330
I don't know if it's true, but it's about,

00:00:03.330 --> 00:00:04.233
yes, with you.

00:00:05.100 --> 00:00:06.030
With Sir Rod.

00:00:06.030 --> 00:00:08.550
So, the first time you
saw the Rolling Stones,

00:00:08.550 --> 00:00:10.800
they were doing blues
music at like a little,

00:00:10.800 --> 00:00:12.150
was it like a pub or theater?

00:00:12.150 --> 00:00:12.983
What was it?

00:00:12.983 --> 00:00:14.456
- Oh, it was a place
called Eel Pie Island.

00:00:14.456 --> 00:00:16.470
It was a little ballroom in Twickenham

00:00:16.470 --> 00:00:18.891
and there was 12 people there.

00:00:18.891 --> 00:00:20.130
- 12 people.
- 12 people.

00:00:20.130 --> 00:00:24.210
And Mick's girlfriend was a
girl called Chrissy Shrimpton,

00:00:24.210 --> 00:00:26.880
who's a sister of the great
model, Jean Shrimpton.

00:00:26.880 --> 00:00:29.850
And my girlfriend, his
girlfriend were friends

00:00:29.850 --> 00:00:31.777
and they said, "Come and see my singer,

00:00:31.777 --> 00:00:33.124
"my boyfriend, he's a singer."

00:00:33.124 --> 00:00:35.010
She said, "Oh, my
boyfriend's a singer, too."

00:00:35.010 --> 00:00:36.300
So, I went over there and watched

00:00:36.300 --> 00:00:37.950
and there was literally nobody there.

00:00:37.950 --> 00:00:40.984
And they were all sitting
on stools playing, you know.

00:00:40.984 --> 00:00:42.615
- But they were doing like blues music?

00:00:42.615 --> 00:00:43.448
- Yeah.

00:00:43.448 --> 00:00:44.281
Oh yeah, yeah.

00:00:44.281 --> 00:00:46.140
Brian Jones was in the band then.

00:00:46.140 --> 00:00:49.500
Ane then within six months to a year bash,

00:00:49.500 --> 00:00:50.782
that was it, they took off.

00:00:50.782 --> 00:00:53.250
- Yeah, those moments are just so cool.

00:00:53.250 --> 00:00:55.440
Like once again, like you
busking and people not knowing

00:00:55.440 --> 00:00:56.273
and then you sitting there

00:00:56.273 --> 00:00:57.106
and not knowing.
- Yeah.

00:00:57.106 --> 00:00:58.409
- What that band would become, yeah.

00:00:58.409 --> 00:00:59.850
It's incredible.
- I think the blues

00:00:59.850 --> 00:01:00.870
in Britain was a big thing,

00:01:00.870 --> 00:01:02.490
so that's where I started as well.

00:01:02.490 --> 00:01:04.050
The playing little pubs,
playing blues stuff,

00:01:04.050 --> 00:01:04.883
'cause that's what we all heard.

00:01:04.883 --> 00:01:07.432
It was a thing you got people dancing.

00:01:07.432 --> 00:01:08.356
- [Kelly] 'Cause it makes such an impact.

00:01:08.356 --> 00:01:09.330
Yeah.
- Yeah, yeah.

00:01:09.330 --> 00:01:10.860
- Like here, there's a lot of music

00:01:10.860 --> 00:01:12.570
you just listen to for
fun, but not much that,

00:01:12.570 --> 00:01:13.403
I mean, feels like

00:01:13.403 --> 00:01:14.340
really moves you.
- Yeah.

00:01:14.340 --> 00:01:16.490
- Yeah, or that's what
I like to listen to.

